{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"body":"Correction to a grounded assumption, found during implementation. The plan stated that finding locations are repository-relative by the time the gate sees them because restore_paths rewrites pod paths. That is wrong. _restore_path in services/orchestration/gates/scanner_pod.py rewrites a pod location onto the worker checkout, which makes it ABSOLUTE, not repository-relative. Subprocess mode does emit repository-relative paths. Attribution therefore normalises both forms by stripping the checkout prefix when present, covered by test_a_pod_mode_location_is_matched_against_the_checkout_relative_path.\n\nTwo further corrections came out of code review. The diff range is three-dot, not two-dot, so base branch churn after branch-off is not attributed to the change. The diff is read NUL separated, because core.quotePath C-quotes any path outside ASCII and such a path would never match the location a scanner reported for the same file."},"env_id":"8c3ef925-fbdc-4d88-8d59-f391cf59568c","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789459069771484001,"uuid":"a8097773-b8f0-4203-9dec-ff710104552f"}